3.2 Non-Commercial Use. "Non-Commercial Use" means only the following:

(a) Personal Use: use by an individual, acting solely on that individual's own behalf, for personal hobby projects or personal learning, that is not undertaken in the course of any trade, business, profession, or employment, is not undertaken for, on behalf of, at the direction of, or for the benefit of any Organization or client, does not involve software, systems, data, or equipment owned, supplied, or obtained through an employer, client, or other Organization, and does not involve providing Output, or services based on the Software or Output, to any Organization, or for the benefit of any Organization at its request or under any arrangement with it. Publishing a Publication to the general public, without any such request or arrangement, is not providing Output to an Organization. Learning undertaken on the individual's own time, with the individual's own resources, does not become Commercial Use merely because the individual later applies general skills in employment.

(b) Independent Security Research: an individual's own independent security research, including coordinated disclosure of findings to an affected vendor, that satisfies the conditions of Section 3.2(a) and is not undertaken to obtain a bug bounty, fee, prize, or other compensation, to sell or license findings or exploits, or as a deliverable for any person. Research concerning a target within the scope of a published bug-bounty, reward, or prize program, or findings submitted through such a program or a reward platform, is presumed to be undertaken to obtain compensation. Research does not cease to qualify merely because the affected vendor later offers an unsolicited reward that the individual did not seek when undertaking the research and that was not offered through such a program, but the individual's acceptance of any reward for findings obtained through the Software is Commercial Use requiring a license for that Use.

(c) Educational Use: use by enrolled students and by faculty and staff of a Qualifying Educational Institution for teaching, coursework, and academic research of that institution, provided the use is not sponsored, commissioned, or funded by a For-Profit Organization for its commercial benefit, is not directed to commercialization, and is not a paid service to any person.

(d) Nonprofit Research: research conducted by a Qualifying Nonprofit in furtherance of its charitable, educational, or scientific mission, provided the research is not a paid service, is not conducted for or funded by a For-Profit Organization for its commercial benefit, and its results are not sold or licensed for a fee or provided to any For-Profit Organization on an exclusive, preferential, confidential, or advance basis.

(e) Bona Fide Journalism, as defined in Section 5.

3.3 Commercial Use. Except for Use that satisfies Section 3.2(c), 3.2(d), or 3.2(e), "Commercial Use" means any Use of the Software or Output that (a) is by, for, on behalf of, or for the benefit of a For-Profit Organization, (b) is undertaken in the course of any trade, business, profession, or employment, (c) is undertaken for compensation or other commercial advantage, or (d) develops, supports, markets, operates, or is incorporated into any commercial product or service. Commercial Use includes internal security, incident response, forensics, software recovery, reverse engineering, malware analysis, research, development, testing, and evaluation by or for a For-Profit Organization, even if no product is sold and no fee is charged; Use by employees, contractors, consultants, and agents in that capacity; consulting, penetration testing, litigation support, expert work, and other client services; work undertaken to obtain a bug bounty or other reward; paid courses, training, and content whose value substantially derives from the Software or Output; developing, distributing, offering, or operating, for a charge or other commercial purpose, any product, plugin, wrapper, script, notebook, container definition, integration, or service that retrieves, installs, invokes, or depends on the Software, including where each end user obtains the Software separately; continuous-integration, build, test, or automated pipelines operated by or for a For-Profit Organization; and any Use described in Section 5.3. Use that is Commercial Use under this Section does not qualify under Section 3.2(a) or 3.2(b). Charging no fee for a particular engagement, using a personal device or account, or describing the activity as research, education, or journalism does not exclude Commercial Use. A Publication made available without charge to the general public, without any request by or arrangement with a For-Profit Organization, does not by that fact alone benefit a For-Profit Organization for p